		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Reported: SL2 ATR is currently showing "Both Units Active Fault". </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Findings:  The Active signal hardwired to the remote I/O at HBS7 panel, Rack 1, module 2, bit 30 and bit 31.</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Remedy: There should only one be active controller. Both should not be active at the same time. Once a full power cycle of this ATR was completed. This reset the redundancy and only one controller was active, and the fault was be cleared.</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">24/08: </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">SL2 ATR is currently showing "Both Units Active Fault". </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Initially I wasn't sure what this fault is but I can confirm the ATR is still able to scan tags because the tags that get read are being updated on the ATR popup.</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Digging deeper into the code to find out what triggers this fault, is when both controllers are active.</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">And they are driven by the Active signal hardwired to the remote I/O at HBS7 panel, Rack 1, module 2, bit 30 and bit 31.</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">This ATR has redundancy, meaning it has two controllers. Normally, at any one time there should only one be active. It's unsure why both are active at the same time (may be a power glitch?), but anyhow, when the operation is finished, please do a complete power cycle of this ATR. This should reset the redundancy and only one controller will be active, and the fault will be cleared.</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">However, if it's still showing the fault on SCADA, then it might be worth to check those two PLC inputs that the controllers are indeed giving you the active signal (just to rule out the PLC inputs aren't faulty which giving us a permanent 24V signal). </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">If confirmed PLC inputs are ok and after power cycle still showing the fault then please call SICK to come in a service the unit.</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="46" ss:MergeAcross="14"/>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="23" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">177246 - Recurring Pulse Wheel Fault, Likely Motor Feedback Issue</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
