		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="39" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">TEMPS D'INTERVENTION / INTERVENTION TIME</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="40" ss:MergeAcross="1">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Date / Date</Data>
			</Cell>
			<Cell ss:Index="3" ss:StyleID="40" ss:MergeAcross="5">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Intervenant / Resource</Data>
			</Cell>
			<Cell ss:Index="9" ss:StyleID="40" ss:MergeAcross="1">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Durée / Duration</Data>
			</Cell>
			<Cell ss:Index="11" ss:StyleID="40" ss:MergeAcross="4">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Type horaire / Hour type</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="41" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Temps passé total / Total time spent : </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="43" ss:MergeAcross="14"/>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="44" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">DETAIL DE L'INTERVENTION / WORK DETAILS</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Help:</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Reported: T110 conveyor tripping on pulse wheel fault repeatedly (8–10 times), requiring a 5-minute system shutdown to recover each time.</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Findings: When the fault occurred, the belt was not physically attempting to run at all. This indicated the root cause was likely a motor feedback fault rather than a genuine pulse wheel fault — if the belt does not run, no pulses are generated, causing a false pulse wheel fault. Code review confirmed the pulse wheel fault timer was set to trigger after 1 second, while the motor feedback fault timer was set to 4.5 seconds, meaning pulse wheel fault was always being raised first regardless of the actual cause.</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Remedy: Motor feedback fault timer in the code adjusted from 4.5 seconds to 0.7 seconds on T110, ensuring motor feedback fault will now trigger before the pulse wheel fault when the belt fails to run. This will allow correct diagnosis going forward. Belt currently running without issue. Shane and Jason Bray to investigate the underlying motor fault when it next occurs.</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">29/08:</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Conveyer T110 coming up with Pulse Wheel Fault</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Site reported T110 tripping on pulse wheel fault again for 8-10 times and they had to shut down the system for 5 mins and then it was working again. </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">I asked them when they reset the fault, was the belt physically trying to run at all and the said no. </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">I talked to Shane and said probably no point for him to go there but I told him to have a chat with Jason Bray and see what the issue might be. </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">I've also checked the code, currently pulse wheel triggers after one second and motor running feedback fault triggers after 4.5 secs. This is a problem because the belt could have been a motor feedback fault but falsely reported as pulse wheel fault. (Well if it doesn't run you won't get pulses right?)</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Hence, I modified the code so that this belt triggers motor fault at 0.7 sec so that we know if it's not running it gives motor feedback fault and not pulse wheel fault (so that we aren't trying to diagnose a wrong problem). </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">It's running fine now but when it doesn't, I believe it's going to be motor fault and not pulse wheel fault.  Shane and Jason will need to look into why. </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Monday 31st August </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Blair and his team might be better placed to help you with this.</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Always difficult when things not new. Yes VFDs if left unpowered for long periods sat on a shelf can deteriorate.</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Also, if the VFD was previously used and removed, why was it removed? I would suggest replacing with known good VFD if unsure.</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Some other thoughts:</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Is the present fault the same as before motor and VFD changed?</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Is the motor pulsing?</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">I see there is a relay that operates the run to the VFD, is this operating correctly? No chattering, coil not getting hot over time and then dropping in and out?</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">If same fault as previously, are you sure there is no mechanical issue? Take motor off and run disconnected via VFD, does same fault occur?</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">If it taking a while for fault to occur after start up, are there any bearing issues – starting to stick when getting hot?</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">I take it when you say pulse wheel ruled out, this is because it has been changed, with cabling and terminations checked.</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="46" ss:MergeAcross="14"/>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="23" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">177249 - roller door is actually closed but the prox isn't hit</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="24" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">   </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="25" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">INFORMATIONS GÉNÉRALES / GENERAL INFORMATION</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
