				<Data ss:Type="String">DETAIL DE L'INTERVENTION / WORK DETAILS</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="52" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Reported:</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="50">
				<Data ss:Type="String">•</Data>
			</Cell>
			<Cell ss:Index="2" ss:StyleID="50" ss:MergeAcross="13">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Site reported TC2 completely down with multiple faults showing on SCADA</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="50">
				<Data ss:Type="String">•</Data>
			</Cell>
			<Cell ss:Index="2" ss:StyleID="50" ss:MergeAcross="13">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Faults included a fuse fault and several Emergency Stop faults (RE102CSR_F, RE102CS_F, TC213_TECH_F, CC102CS_F, X2_040Q6_SF_F)</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="50">
				<Data ss:Type="String">•</Data>
			</Cell>
			<Cell ss:Index="2" ss:StyleID="50" ss:MergeAcross="13">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Fault pattern similar to a previous occurrence</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="52" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Findings:</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="50">
				<Data ss:Type="String">•</Data>
			</Cell>
			<Cell ss:Index="2" ss:StyleID="50" ss:MergeAcross="13">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Initial fuse fault indication (X2_040Q6_SF_F) suggested a blown fuse, consistent with the prior incident</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="50">
				<Data ss:Type="String">•</Data>
			</Cell>
			<Cell ss:Index="2" ss:StyleID="50" ss:MergeAcross="13">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Site confirmed no fuses were physically blown</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="50">
				<Data ss:Type="String">•</Data>
			</Cell>
			<Cell ss:Index="2" ss:StyleID="50" ss:MergeAcross="13">
				<Data ss:Type="String">PLC showed no I/O card faults, ruling out a rack/comms issue</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="50">
				<Data ss:Type="String">•</Data>
			</Cell>
			<Cell ss:Index="2" ss:StyleID="50" ss:MergeAcross="13">
				<Data ss:Type="String">With fuses intact and no I/O faults, root cause was assessed as loss of 24VDC supply rather than a fuse or wiring fault</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="50">
				<Data ss:Type="String">•</Data>
			</Cell>
			<Cell ss:Index="2" ss:StyleID="50" ss:MergeAcross="13">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Downstream E-stop-related faults were a knock-on effect of the 24V loss on that circuit (monitored NC loops read as open when 24V dropped, not from an actual E-stop press)</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="50">
				<Data ss:Type="String">•</Data>
			</Cell>
			<Cell ss:Index="2" ss:StyleID="50" ss:MergeAcross="13">
				<Data ss:Type="String">System recovered when technician went online to the PLC; site subsequently confirmed the 24VDC power supply was faulty</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="50">
				<Data ss:Type="String">•</Data>
			</Cell>
			<Cell ss:Index="2" ss:StyleID="50" ss:MergeAcross="13">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Faulty 24V power supply was replaced on site, after which all faults cleared</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="52" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Remedy:</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="50">
				<Data ss:Type="String">•</Data>
			</Cell>
			<Cell ss:Index="2" ss:StyleID="50" ss:MergeAcross="13">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Faulty 24VDC power supply identified and replaced by site</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="50">
				<Data ss:Type="String">•</Data>
			</Cell>
			<Cell ss:Index="2" ss:StyleID="50" ss:MergeAcross="13">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Followed up with site (Udit) via email requesting further detail: which specific supply was replaced, visible signs of failure, condition/whereabouts of the faulty unit, any preceding anomalies (power outages, voltage spikes, panel work), and unit age — to determine if this is an isolated failure or a broader concern</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="50">
				<Data ss:Type="String">•</Data>
			</Cell>
			<Cell ss:Index="2" ss:StyleID="50" ss:MergeAcross="13">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Noted for future reference: "fuse fault" alarms on this system indicate loss of 24V at a monitored point, which can be caused by either a blown fuse or a failed power supply — troubleshooting should check the supply output voltage, not just physical fuses, when I/O faults are absent</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">27/08:</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Glidepath system is down at airport</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Site reported TC2 was completely down and there was whole bunch of faults showing up similar to last time. According to Tiaan's screenshot there was fuse faults and PLC showed no I/O faults. My first guess was blown fuse like last time but Tiaan confirmed with site there's no fuse blown. In that case they must have lost 24V, which most likely a power supply issue.</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">As soon as I finished my site induction I went online to the PLC and the system suddenly came back to normal. I called back to site to confirm the case and that they discovered the 24V power supply was faulty. Replaced it and all the faults were gone.</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Next time if similar issue happen, it usually relates to 24V supply, either blown fuse or faulty power supply.</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="46" ss:MergeAcross="14"/>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="23" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">177537 - Motor Fault on Outbound Carousel</Data>
