		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">27/08</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Reported: Wellington Airport reported a “Voltage Monitor Relay Fault” alarm on TC1 SCADA. The issue had been occurring since 25 August but was not impacting operations.</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Findings: Remote checks of SCADA showed no active TC1 alarms at the time of investigation. The site advised that an electrician attended shortly after the call and made an adjustment to the voltage.</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String">Remedy: The voltage adjustment resolved the alarm, and the system returned to normal operation.</Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
		<Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
			<Cell ss:Index="1" ss:StyleID="45" ss:MergeAcross="14">
				<Data ss:Type="String"> </Data>
			</Cell>
		</Row>
